**Behavior implemented:**
- `-m MODE`, `-mMODE`, `--mode MODE`, `--mode=MODE` with last-mode-wins
- Numeric modes (octal 0000–7777): 4-or-fewer digits preserve inherited special bits; 5+ digits clear unspecified special bits
- Symbolic modes: full GNU Coreutils 9.11 directory semantics starting from `a=rwx` (0o777)
  - u/g/o/a/omitted who selectors, `+`/`-`/`=` operators
  - rwxXst permissions, permission-copy (`g=u`), comma-separated clauses
  - Empty assignments (`o=`) valid; empty whole argument rejected
  - Umask interaction: explicit who unaffected; omitted who `+`/`-` masked by `~umask`; omitted who `=` filters by `~umask`
